    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# 04 — Fine-tune + Phase 5.9 (RAG metrics + GitHub push)\n",
        "\n",
        "Single Kaggle notebook that:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Builds the Phase 1 grounded dataset (public fixtures)\n",
        "2. Runs **QLoRA SFT** (Unsloth, seed `3407`)\n",
        "3. Builds hybrid RAG corpus + index + eval set\n",
        "4. Writes **real** `manifest.json` / `rag_metrics.json` / `rag_generation_metrics.json`\n",
        "5. Fills `RAG_EVAL_REPORT.md` + README Results from those JSON files only\n",
        "6. Optionally publishes the adapter to Hugging Face\n",
        "7. Pushes metrics + report updates to GitHub (`main`)\n",
        "\n",
        "**Defaults are safe.** Flip flags only on a **Kaggle T4**. Do not invent percentages.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Flag | Default | Purpose |\n",
        "|------|---------|---------|\n",
        "| `RUN_TRAIN` | `False` | Real Unsloth train |\n",
        "| `MAX_STEPS` | `60` | Smoke steps; set `None` for full epoch from YAML |\n",
        "| `RUN_RAG` | `False` | ST embeddings + retrieval + generate eval |\n",
        "| `PUBLISH_HF` | `False` | Upload adapter (needs `HF_TOKEN` secret) |\n",
        "| `PUSH_GITHUB` | `False` | Commit metrics/report to `main` (needs `GITHUB_TOKEN`) |\n",
        "\n",
        "Secrets (Kaggle → Add-ons → Secrets): `HF_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` (classic PAT with `repo` scope). Never paste tokens into cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 0. Knobs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import json\n",
        "from datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\n",
        "\n",
        "# --- Edit these ---\n",
        "RUN_TRAIN = False          # True = Unsloth QLoRA train (GPU)\n",
        "MAX_STEPS = 60             # smoke; set None for full epoch from YAML\n",
        "MAX_SAMPLES = 8            # fixture samples per public source\n",
        "DOWNLOAD_HF = False        # optional tiny HF stream\n",
        "CONFIG_PATH = \"configs/default.yaml\"  # or configs/llama32-8b.yaml\n",
        "\n",
        "RUN_RAG = False            # True = ST embed + retrieval + generate eval\n",
        "PUBLISH_HF = False         # True = push adapter to Hub\n",
        "PUSH_GITHUB = False        # True = git commit+push metrics/report to main\n",
        "\n",
        "HF_REPO_ID = \"nuwanda94/llama32-3b-ecra-sft\"\n",
        "GITHUB_OWNER = \"nuwanda94\"\n",
        "GITHUB_REPO = \"earnings-call-research-assistant\"\n",
        "GITHUB_BRANCH = \"main\"\n",
        "ADAPTER_DIR = Path(\"outputs/adapters/llama32-3b-ecra-sft\")\n",
        "\n",
        "IST = timezone(timedelta(hours=5, minutes=30))\n",
        "NOW_IST = datetime.now(IST).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M IST\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"RUN_TRAIN\", RUN_TRAIN, \"MAX_STEPS\", MAX_STEPS)\n",
        "print(\"RUN_RAG\", RUN_RAG, \"PUBLISH_HF\", PUBLISH_HF, \"PUSH_GITHUB\", PUSH_GITHUB)\n",
        "print(\"NOW_IST\", NOW_IST)"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Clone repo + installs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "IN_KAGGLE = Path(\"/kaggle\").exists()\n",
        "print(\"IN_KAGGLE:\", IN_KAGGLE)\n",
        "\n",
        "if IN_KAGGLE:\n",
        "    work = Path(\"/kaggle/working\")\n",
        "    repo = work / \"earnings-call-research-assistant\"\n",
        "    if not (repo / \"src\" / \"earnings_call_research_assistant\" / \"inference.py\").exists():\n",
        "        %cd /kaggle/working\n",
        "        !git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/nuwanda94/earnings-call-research-assistant.git\n",
        "        repo = work / \"earnings-call-research-assistant\"\n",
        "    REPO = repo.resolve()\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    REPO = Path(\"..\").resolve()\n",
        "    if not (REPO / \"src\" / \"earnings_call_research_assistant\").is_dir():\n",
        "        REPO = Path.cwd().resolve()\n",
        "\n",
        "SRC = REPO / \"src\"\n",
        "assert (SRC / \"earnings_call_research_assistant\" / \"inference.py\").exists(), SRC\n",
        "if str(SRC) not in sys.path:\n",
        "    sys.path.insert(0, str(SRC))\n",
        "os.chdir(REPO)\n",
        "print(\"REPO:\", REPO)\n",
        "print(\"cwd:\", Path.cwd())\n",
        "\n",
        "import earnings_call_research_assistant as ecra\n",
        "print(\"package:\", getattr(ecra, \"__version__\", \"?\"), ecra.__file__)"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "if IN_KAGGLE:\n",
        "    %pip install -q pyyaml rank_bm25\n",
        "    if RUN_TRAIN or RUN_RAG:\n",
        "        %pip install -q unsloth transformers accelerate bitsandbytes datasets trl peft sentence-transformers\n",
        "    if PUBLISH_HF:\n",
        "        %pip install -q huggingface_hub\n",
        "print(\"installs done\")"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Load secrets (never print values)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def _load_secret(name: str) -> bool:\n",
        "    if os.environ.get(name):\n",
        "        print(f\"{name}: already in env\")\n",
        "        return True\n",
        "    if not IN_KAGGLE:\n",
        "        print(f\"{name}: not set (local)\")\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\n",
        "        val = UserSecretsClient().get_secret(name)\n",
        "        if val:\n",
        "            os.environ[name] = val\n",
        "            print(f\"{name}: loaded from Kaggle secrets\")\n",
        "            return True\n",
        "        print(f\"{name}: secret empty\")\n",
        "    except Exception as exc:\n",
        "        print(f\"{name}: {type(exc).__name__}\")\n",
        "    return False\n",
        "\n",
        "has_hf = _load_secret(\"HF_TOKEN\") or _load_secret(\"HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN\")\n",
        "has_gh = _load_secret(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\")\n",
        "print(\"has_hf\", has_hf, \"has_gh\", has_gh)"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Phase 1 — data foundation (public fixtures)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from earnings_call_research_assistant.data import (\n",
        "    ingest_catalog,\n",
        "    write_jsonl,\n",
        "    ChunkConfig,\n",
        "    chunk_records,\n",
        "    write_chunks_jsonl,\n",
        "    GenerateConfig,\n",
        "    generate_pairs,\n",
        "    write_pairs_jsonl,\n",
        "    FilterConfig,\n",
        "    filter_pairs,\n",
        "    write_filter_report,\n",
        "    DATASET_VERSION,\n",
        "    SelectConfig,\n",
        "    select_and_split,\n",
        "    write_splits,\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "RAW = Path(\"data/raw/public_sample.jsonl\")\n",
        "CHUNKS = Path(\"data/processed/chunks.jsonl\")\n",
        "PAIRS = Path(\"data/processed/grounded_pairs.jsonl\")\n",
        "FILTERED = Path(\"data/processed/filtered_pairs.jsonl\")\n",
        "OUT_DIR = Path(\"data/processed\") / DATASET_VERSION\n",
        "\n",
        "records = ingest_catalog(max_samples=MAX_SAMPLES, download=DOWNLOAD_HF)\n",
        "write_jsonl(records, RAW)\n",
        "print(f\"ingest: {len(records)} -> {RAW}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "chunks = chunk_records(records, config=ChunkConfig(window_sentences=4, stride_sentences=2))\n",
        "write_chunks_jsonl(chunks, CHUNKS)\n",
        "print(f\"chunks: {len(chunks)} -> {CHUNKS}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "pairs = generate_pairs(chunks, config=GenerateConfig(max_qa_per_chunk=2, include_summary=True, use_llm=False))\n",
        "write_pairs_jsonl(pairs, PAIRS)\n",
        "print(f\"pairs: {len(pairs)} -> {PAIRS}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "kept, report = filter_pairs(\n",
        "    pairs,\n",
        "    config=FilterConfig(min_output_chars=40, near_dup_jaccard=0.88, use_llm_judge=False),\n",
        ")\n",
        "write_pairs_jsonl(kept, FILTERED)\n",
        "write_filter_report(report, Path(\"data/processed/filter_report.json\"))\n",
        "print(f\"filtered: in={report.n_in} kept={report.n_kept}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sel_cfg = SelectConfig(\n",
        "    target_min=1,\n",
        "    target_max=6000,\n",
        "    max_per_source=2500,\n",
        "    diversity_jaccard_cap=0.72,\n",
        "    seed=94,\n",
        "    dataset_version=DATASET_VERSION,\n",
        ")\n",
        "splits, sel_report = select_and_split(kept, config=sel_cfg)\n",
        "paths = write_splits(splits, OUT_DIR, report=sel_report, config=sel_cfg)\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"splits: train={sel_report.n_train} val={sel_report.n_val} test={sel_report.n_test} \"\n",
        "    f\"-> {OUT_DIR}\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "for k, v in paths.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"  {k}: {v}\")"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. QLoRA SFT — dry-run always, real train if `RUN_TRAIN`"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from earnings_call_research_assistant.training.sft import run_sft\n",
        "\n",
        "plan = run_sft(\n",
        "    config_path=CONFIG_PATH,\n",
        "    dataset_dir=OUT_DIR,\n",
        "    dry_run=True,\n",
        "    max_steps=MAX_STEPS,\n",
        "    require_train=False,\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\n",
        "    f\"dry_run plan: model={plan.model_name} seed={plan.seed} \"\n",
        "    f\"train={plan.n_train} val={plan.n_val} adapter={plan.adapter_dir}\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"wrote outputs/sft_plan.json\")"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"cuda:\", torch.cuda.is_available(),\n",
        "      torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if not RUN_TRAIN:\n",
        "    print(\"Skipped real train (RUN_TRAIN=False).\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    if not torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(\"RUN_TRAIN=True but no CUDA. Enable Kaggle T4.\")\n",
        "    train_plan = run_sft(\n",
        "        config_path=CONFIG_PATH,\n",
        "        dataset_dir=OUT_DIR,\n",
        "        dry_run=False,\n",
        "        max_steps=MAX_STEPS,\n",
        "        require_train=True,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    print(\"Train finished.\")\n",
        "    print(\"adapter:\", train_plan.adapter_dir)\n",
        "    print(\"exists:\", Path(train_plan.adapter_dir).exists())"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Phase 5 — RAG corpus, index, eval set, metrics"
      ]
